The bug was caused by the premature call to `rcutree_report_cpu_starting()` in the `start_secondary` function of `smp.c`, which occurred before the TLB initialization (`tlb_init()`). This led to access of per-cpu variables that were not yet properly initialized, particularly affecting machines with more than 8 nodes that rely on TLB-based per-cpu base addresses.

